From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mpl: -pdn_min_channel_size proposes a channel when macros do not fit

Halos are often what keeps macros from fitting. With
-pdn_min_channel_size, the narrowest channel the user trusts the PDN to
repair, the MPL-0003 error rebuilds the macro clusters at that channel,
through the clustering engine's own halo rule and the tiling generator,
and says whether it fits or how far the core must grow even at it. The
option changes no placement. Clusters that hold standard cells are shaped
by annealing and get no proposal. The value is the user's: whether the
PDN can repair a channel depends on where its straps fall, not only on
the channel's width, so mpl does not derive it.

Not upstreamed; retires at the //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.

---
diff --git a/src/mpl/README.md b/src/mpl/README.md
index e847eeb6d4..946d952776 100644
--- a/src/mpl/README.md
+++ b/src/mpl/README.md
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@ rtl_macro_placer
     [-coarsening_ratio coarsening_ratio]
     [-large_net_threshold large_net_threshold]
     [-min_channel_size {width [height]}]
+    [-pdn_min_channel_size {width [height]}]
     [-halo_width halo_width]
     [-halo_height halo_height]
     [-fence_lx fence_lx] 
@@ -60,6 +61,7 @@ rtl_macro_placer
 | `-coarsening_ratio` | The larger the coarsening_ratio, the faster the convergence process. The allowed values are floats, and the default value is `10.0`. |
 | `-large_net_threshold` | Ignore nets with many connections during clustering, such as global nets. The default value is `50`, and the allowed values are integers `[0, MAX_INT]`. |
 | `-min_channel_size` | Minimum channel width and height between macros (microns), given as `{width}` or `{width height}`. If `height` is omitted, it defaults to `width`. The default value is `0.0` for both. |
+| `-pdn_min_channel_size` | The narrowest channel between macros that the PDN can repair (microns), given as `{width}` or `{width height}`. It does not change the placement: when the macros do not fit, the error proposes this channel, or says how far the outline must grow even at it. |
 | `-halo_width`, `-halo_height` | **Deprecated: use `-min_channel_size` instead.** Horizontal/vertical halo around macros (microns), applied uniformly on all sides. Equivalent to `-min_channel_size {2*halo_width 2*halo_height}`. |
 | `-fence_lx`, `-fence_ly`, `-fence_ux`, `-fence_uy` | Defines the global fence bounding box coordinates. The default values are the core area coordinates. |
 | `-target_util` | Specifies the target utilization. The allowed values are floats and the default value is `0.25`. |
@@ -179,6 +181,10 @@ bazelisk test //src/mpl/...
   budget. A problem it cannot decide within that budget gets the error
   without a proof; this happens when the macros fill nearly all of the
   outline (on the ORFS designs, one problem at 99% fill).
+- `-pdn_min_channel_size` is given by the user. mpl does not derive it from
+  the PDN: whether the PDN can repair a channel depends on where its straps
+  fall relative to the channel, not only on the channel's width, and mpl
+  runs before the PDN is defined.
 
